tely.\n- Escalate deterioration or danger signs promptly.\n\n## 5. Quick Revision\n**Definition → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Growth and development.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Growth and development.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Growth and development.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="ANM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="Child Health Nursing" and c.chapter_no=1 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
insert into public.library_materials(course,year_level,semester,subject,material_type,title,description,provider,sort_order,is_active,chapter_id,content_body) select "ANM","1st Year",null,"Child Health Nursing",'Study Notes',"Chapter 2: Essential newborn care — Study Notes","Original detailed study notes with objectives, core concepts, nursing responsibilities, revision and MCQs.",'Bhumi Nursing College',360,true,c.id,"# Essential newborn care\n\n## 1. Overview\nThis chapter covers **Essential newborn care** under **Child Health Nursing**. The main nursing focus is safe patient care, assessment, nursing process, communication and documentation. Study the topic by linking theory with assessment, prevention, patient education and safe practice.\n\n## 2. Learning Objectives\n- Define and explain the topic in simple nursing language.\n- Identify its major principles, components and terminology.\n- Describe relevant nursing assessment and responsibilities.\n- Recognize important risks or danger signs requiring review or referral.\n- Apply the concept while protecting safety, dignity, privacy and confidentiality.\n\n## 3. Core Study Notes\nEssential newborn care includes warmth, breathing assessment, clean cord care, early breastfeeding support, infection prevention and observation for danger signs.\n\nFor nursing practice, use the nursing-process approach: **assessment → identification of needs/problems → planning → implementation → evaluation**, followed by accurate documentation and communication.\n\n## 4. Nursing Responsibilities\n- Perform appropriate assessment and identify abnormal findings.\n- Follow hand hygiene, standard precautions and patient-safety principles.\n- Explain care clearly and protect privacy and dignity.\n- Work within scope of practice and institutional protocols.\n- Document relevant findings and interventions accurately.\n- Escalate deterioration or danger signs promptly.\n\n## 5. Quick Revision\n**Definition → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Essential newborn care.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Essential newborn care.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Essential newborn care.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="ANM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="Child Health Nursing" and c.chapter_no=2 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
insert into public.library_materials(course,year_level,semester,subject,material_type,title,description,provider,sort_order,is_active,chapter_id,content_body) select "ANM","1st Year",null,"Child Health Nursing",'Study Notes',"Chapter 3: Breastfeeding — Study Notes","Original detailed study notes with objectives, core concepts, nursing responsibilities, revision and MCQs.",'Bhumi Nursing College',370,true,c.id,"# Breastfeeding\n\n## 1. Overview\nThis chapter covers **Breastfeeding** under **Child Health Nursing**. The main nursing focus is safe patient care, assessment, nursing process, communication and documentation. Study the topic by linking theory with assessment, prevention, patient education and safe practice.\n\n## 2. Learning Objectives\n- Define and explain the topic in simple nursing language.\n- Identify its major principles, components and terminology.\n- Describe relevant nursing assessment and responsibilities.\n- Recognize important risks or danger signs requiring review or referral.\n- Apply the concept while protecting safety, dignity, privacy and confidentiality.\n\n## 3. Core Study Notes\nBreastfeeding supports infant nutrition, immunity and bonding. Counselling includes early initiation when clinically appropriate, correct positioning and attachment, feeding to infant cues, monitoring output and growth, and identifying feeding problems.\n\nFor nursing practice, use the nursing-process approach: **assessment → identification of needs/problems → planning → implementation → evaluation**, followed by accurate documentation and communication.\n\n## 4. Nursing Responsibilities\n- Perform appropriate assessment and identify abnormal findings.\n- Follow hand hygiene, standard precautions and patient-safety principles.\n- Explain care clearly and protect privacy and dignity.\n- Work within scope of practice and institutional protocols.\n- Document relevant findings and interventions accurately.\n- Escalate deterioration or danger signs promptly.\n\n## 5. Quick Revision\n**Definition → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Breastfeeding.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Breastfeeding.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Breastfeeding.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="ANM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="Child Health Nursing" and c.chapter_no=3 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
