 → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Infection and disease.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Infection and disease.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Infection and disease.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="GNM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="Microbiology" and c.chapter_no=9 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
insert into public.library_materials(course,year_level,semester,subject,material_type,title,description,provider,sort_order,is_active,chapter_id,content_body) select "GNM","1st Year",null,"Microbiology",'Study Notes',"Chapter 10: Immunity — Study Notes","Original detailed study notes with objectives, core concepts, nursing responsibilities, revision and MCQs.",'Bhumi Nursing College',1090,true,c.id,"# Immunity\n\n## 1. Overview\nThis chapter covers **Immunity** under **Microbiology**. The main nursing focus is microorganisms, transmission, prevention and infection-control relevance. Study the topic by linking theory with assessment, prevention, patient education and safe practice.\n\n## 2. Learning Objectives\n- Define and explain the topic in simple nursing language.\n- Identify its major principles, components and terminology.\n- Describe relevant nursing assessment and responsibilities.\n- Recognize important risks or danger signs requiring review or referral.\n- Apply the concept while protecting safety, dignity, privacy and confidentiality.\n\n## 3. Core Study Notes\nBegin with the definition and scope, then study the major components, normal principles or expected findings, factors affecting the topic, common problems and appropriate nursing responses. Connect classroom knowledge with clinical observation, prevention, patient education and documentation.\n\nFor nursing practice, use the nursing-process approach: **assessment → identification of needs/problems → planning → implementation → evaluation**, followed by accurate documentation and communication.\n\n## 4. Nursing Responsibilities\n- Perform appropriate assessment and identify abnormal findings.\n- Follow hand hygiene, standard precautions and patient-safety principles.\n- Explain care clearly and protect privacy and dignity.\n- Work within scope of practice and institutional protocols.\n- Document relevant findings and interventions accurately.\n- Escalate deterioration or danger signs promptly.\n\n## 5. Quick Revision\n**Definition → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Immunity.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Immunity.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Immunity.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="GNM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="Microbiology" and c.chapter_no=10 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
insert into public.library_materials(course,year_level,semester,subject,material_type,title,description,provider,sort_order,is_active,chapter_id,content_body) select "GNM","1st Year",null,"Microbiology",'Study Notes',"Chapter 11: Sterilization and disinfection — Study Notes","Original detailed study notes with objectives, core concepts, nursing responsibilities, revision and MCQs.",'Bhumi Nursing College',1100,true,c.id,"# Sterilization and disinfection\n\n## 1. Overview\nThis chapter covers **Sterilization and disinfection** under **Microbiology**. The main nursing focus is microorganisms, transmission, prevention and infection-control relevance. Study the topic by linking theory with assessment, prevention, patient education and safe practice.\n\n## 2. Learning Objectives\n- Define and explain the topic in simple nursing language.\n- Identify its major principles, components and terminology.\n- Describe relevant nursing assessment and responsibilities.\n- Recognize important risks or danger signs requiring review or referral.\n- Apply the concept while protecting safety, dignity, privacy and confidentiality.\n\n## 3. Core Study Notes\nInfection prevention uses hand hygiene, standard precautions, appropriate PPE, safe injection practice, respiratory hygiene, environmental cleaning and correct sharps/biomedical-waste handling.\n\nFor nursing practice, use the nursing-process approach: **assessment → identification of needs/problems → planning → implementation → evaluation**, followed by accurate documentation and communication.\n\n## 4. Nursing Responsibilities\n- Perform appropriate assessment and identify abnormal findings.\n- Follow hand hygiene, standard precautions and patient-safety principles.\n- Explain care clearly and protect privacy and dignity.\n- Work within scope of practice and institutional protocols.\n- Document relevant findings and interventions accurately.\n- Escalate deterioration or danger signs promptly.\n\n## 5. Quick Revision\n**Definition → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Sterilization and disinfection.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Sterilization and disinfection.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Sterilization and disinfection.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="GNM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="Microbiology" and c.chapter_no=11 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
