scalate deterioration or danger signs promptly.\n\n## 5. Quick Revision\n**Definition → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Basic procedures.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Basic procedures.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Basic procedures.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="GNM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="Fundamentals of Nursing" and c.chapter_no=20 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
insert into public.library_materials(course,year_level,semester,subject,material_type,title,description,provider,sort_order,is_active,chapter_id,content_body) select "GNM","1st Year",null,"First Aid",'Study Notes',"Chapter 1: Principles of first aid — Study Notes","Original detailed study notes with objectives, core concepts, nursing responsibilities, revision and MCQs.",'Bhumi Nursing College',1610,true,c.id,"# Principles of first aid\n\n## 1. Overview\nThis chapter covers **Principles of first aid** under **First Aid**. The main nursing focus is the concept, its application in nursing practice and safe patient care. Study the topic by linking theory with assessment, prevention, patient education and safe practice.\n\n## 2. Learning Objectives\n- Define and explain the topic in simple nursing language.\n- Identify its major principles, components and terminology.\n- Describe relevant nursing assessment and responsibilities.\n- Recognize important risks or danger signs requiring review or referral.\n- Apply the concept while protecting safety, dignity, privacy and confidentiality.\n\n## 3. Core Study Notes\nFirst aid prioritizes scene safety, rapid assessment, activation of emergency help and life-saving measures within the responder’s training. For suspected cardiac arrest, current basic-life-support guidance should be followed.\n\nFor nursing practice, use the nursing-process approach: **assessment → identification of needs/problems → planning → implementation → evaluation**, followed by accurate documentation and communication.\n\n## 4. Nursing Responsibilities\n- Perform appropriate assessment and identify abnormal findings.\n- Follow hand hygiene, standard precautions and patient-safety principles.\n- Explain care clearly and protect privacy and dignity.\n- Work within scope of practice and institutional protocols.\n- Document relevant findings and interventions accurately.\n- Escalate deterioration or danger signs promptly.\n\n## 5. Quick Revision\n**Definition → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Principles of first aid.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Principles of first aid.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Principles of first aid.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="GNM" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce(null,'') and c.subject="First Aid" and c.chapter_no=1 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
