ion → key principles → assessment → nursing responsibilities → patient education → danger signs/referral → documentation.**\n\n## 6. Important Questions\n1. Define Therapeutic diets.\n2. Explain the major principles/components of Therapeutic diets.\n3. Describe nursing responsibilities related to Therapeutic diets.\n4. What assessment findings are important?\n5. Explain relevant patient/family health education.\n6. List important precautions and safety measures.\n7. When is referral or urgent clinical review required?\n\n## 7. Self-Check MCQs\n1. The first priority in nursing care is: A. Paperwork B. Patient safety C. Saving supplies D. Finishing quickly — **Answer: B**\n2. Accurate documentation mainly supports: A. Continuity and accountability B. Avoiding communication C. Replacing assessment D. Ending follow-up — **Answer: A**\n3. Significant deterioration should be reported: A. At discharge B. Promptly through the clinical chain C. Never D. Next month — **Answer: B**\n4. Health education is stronger when: A. Understanding is checked B. Questions are discouraged C. Language is unnecessarily complex D. Privacy is ignored — **Answer: A**\n5. Infection-prevention practices should be followed: A. Only for visibly infected patients B. According to standard precautions and the care situation C. Only in ICU D. Only in surgery — **Answer: B**\n\n*Original educational notes prepared for Bhumi Nursing College. These notes do not reproduce copyrighted textbook text. For procedures, doses, immunization schedules and emergency care, follow the latest approved institutional and government/clinical guidelines.*" from public.library_chapters c where c.course="B.Sc Nursing" and c.year_level="1st Year" and coalesce(c.semester,'')=coalesce("'Semester 2'",'') and c.subject="Nutrition & Dietetics" and c.chapter_no=8 and not exists (select 1 from public.library_materials m where m.chapter_id=c.id and m.material_type='Study Notes');
